  </data>
  <data name="PrerequisiteSetupWindow_Intro" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>To let Rewind GP automatically set up your races and overlay controls on top of the game, two things need to be configured in AMS2 first:</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrerequisiteSetupWindow_Step1Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>1) Set Telemetry Output to "Project Cars 2"</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrerequisiteSetupWindow_Step1Body" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>In AMS2's Options &gt; Controls (or Gameplay) menu, set the UDP/Telemetry output format to "Project Cars 2" so Rewind GP can read live session data.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrerequisiteSetupWindow_Step2Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>2) Enable Borderless Window mode</value>
  </data>
  <data name="PrerequisiteSetupWindow_Step2Body" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>In AMS2's Options &gt; Video menu, set the display mode to "Borderless Window" so Rewind GP's overlay can appear on top of the game.</value>
  </data>
